{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The vision</b> — the gematria of מראה is 251, equal to גבריאל (Gabriel), which teaches that he was girded with a sort of leather apron and showed Moses the pattern of the Tabernacle and the pattern of all its vessels." "<b>And so shall you make</b> — twice here and the other 'and so shall you make' of Gideon, for the merit of these vessels stood for Gideon, and all the deeds of Gideon were corresponding to the service of the Tabernacle and its vessels. He placed the torches in pitchers to recall the merit of these vessels. And at the beginning of the middle watch, to recall the merit of the Temple service, for then they would clear the ashes from the altar, and it is the first service they would perform in it by day."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:20.802574751Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}